{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1|---\\n2|soterion:\\n3|  sigil: \\\"SCROLL\\\"\\n4|  role: \\\"assessment_plan\\\"\\n5|  owner: \\\"HERMES\\\"\\n6|  status: \\\"draft\\\"\\n7|  reviewed: \\\"2026-10-09\\\"\\n8|---\\n9|\\n10|# INFERENCE_ASSESSMENT\\n11|\\n12|## Current specification: mixed inference and home-server capacity\\n13|\\n14|This section supersedes the earlier general-agent replacement framing and blanket\\n15|no-promotion disposition. Assess and implement useful roles across local inference,\\n16|valid free providers and frontier providers already available through Manwe.\\n17|Core need not own multi-step continuation. A model may qualify for a bounded role\\n18|while failing autonomous coding or research; retain failures at their actual scope.\\n19|Hermes is the worker/conversation harness and Arda retains policy and authority.\\n20|\\n21|Required outcomes:\\n22|- Support concurrent interactive Arandur-oriented conversation, scheduled research,\\n23|  maintenance, tool development, project assessment and essential-service monitoring.\\n24|- Match each job to demonstrated capability, privacy, context, latency, availability\\n25|  and cost; escalate difficult work rather than demand frontier behavior locally.\\n26|- Distinguish catalog presence, authenticated inference access, quota and measured\\n27|  task success. Free-provider labels are not guarantees of continuing availability.\\n28|- Expand Beelink toward a home-server role, not merely another resident model.\\n29|  Inventory storage, services, backups, resource contention and recovery first;\\n30|  preserve reliable home services ahead of optional inference residency.\\n31|- Explore economically useful workflows toward self-sustaining operation and\\n32|  hardware reinvestment. Track costs and realized value; revenue is not assumed.\\n33|  Spending, customer commitments, financial transactions and expanded external\\n34|  authority require explicit operator approval.\\n35|\\n36|Execution order under the operator's plan-adjustment/implementation request:\\n37|1. Refresh Manwe's live provider/capability/access matrix and Beelink's actual\\n38|   resource/service/storage inventory without exposing credentials.\\n39|2. Refresh Hugging Face discovery beyond the previously tested candidates. Pin\\n40|   promising artifacts/licenses/runtime prerequisites per role before downloading.\\n41|3. Qualify bounded local specialist jobs and valid remote escalation routes using\\n42|   existing Manwe/Hermes paths; do not invent a parallel scheduler or authority path.\\n43|4. Exercise mixed concurrent work with bounded queues, priorities, cancellation,\\n44|   latency/cost accounting and fail-closed unavailable-provider behavior.\\n45|5. Promote independently reviewed role-specific improvements incrementally with\\n46|   rollback. Existing model age motivates comparison, not presumed inferiority.\\n47|\\n48|Acceptance: one useful interactive stream can coexist with a scheduled background\\n49|job without unacceptable contention; attribution, outcomes and failures are retained;\\n50|local specialists and remote escalation satisfy their separate contracts. Beelink\\n51|service additions require explicit service selection after inventory, secure network\\n52|exposure and recovery checks. Prior disruption limits remain; this request does not\\n53|permit wiping storage, buying hardware or replacing the entire fleet.\\n54|\\n55|Earlier tests remain evidence, not a requirement that every node become a general\\n56|agent. Full-profile continuation is mandatory only for roles that actually own it.\\n57|\\n58|### Mixed-role execution checkpoint\\n59|\\n60|Current operator direction: retain the routing repairs, candidate evidence and\\n61|useful implementation below; the progress check is not a reset or cancellation.\\n62|Converge on one operating arrangement: desktop GPU reserved for operator use,\\n63|bounded background work on Server, and a demonstrated capable escalation route.\\n64|The operator stopped desktop `mesh-llm`; readback confirms inactive/MainPID=0.\\n65|Do not restart it for qualification. Keep backups and HUD/voice parked.\\n66|Current installed checkpoint: the reviewed Responses body-read timeout repair\\n67|is deployed in supervised child PID 86591 under unchanged Arda PID 2711031;\\n68|[deployment readback](../audits/inference-assessment-2026-10-09/escalation-timeout-deployment.json)\\n69|records hash `464348830f1a9614230624d736abc77fede8ed750b105d65e62ab38a27a49dcb`,\\n70|healthy subscription routing and preserved inactive desktop inference. All 320\\n71|release-mode library tests passed in the exact baseline export plus reviewed\\n72|single-file patch. Body-read timeouts now remain transport errors rather than\\n73|becoming empty malformed payloads; the configurable default allows 120 seconds.\\n74|The [installed Hermes task](../audits/inference-assessment-2026-10-09/subscription-hermes-acceptance.json)\\n75|completed missing-file recovery, evidence reads and report writing in 69.366 seconds.\\n76|The [failed pre-repair task](../audits/inference-assessment-20...", "duration_ms": 266, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791745778290}
